<title>SINGAPORE: SM Summit 1996 net profit up 86 pct.</title>
<headline>SM Summit 1996 net profit up 86 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    10.11  vs    5.45</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     0.50  vs    0.40</p>
<p>    Special dividend (cents)	   0.50  vs     nil</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    5.39  vs    2.90</p>
<p>    Turnover				37.52  vs   21.78</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	0.30  vs    0.09</p>
<p>    Interest expense		     0.60  vs    0.30</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   3.63  vs    2.32</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	    0.62  vs    0.49</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			13.24  vs    6.06</p>
<p>    Tax					3.75  vs    1.10</p>
<p>Note - Full name is SM Summit Holdings. The company makes compact discs.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 870 8090)</p>
</text>
